{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From the Midianites.</b> And not from the Moabites — for the Moabites entered the matter out of fear, for they were afraid that Israel would despoil them, for it was said only ״וְאַל תִּתְגַּר בָּם מִלְחָמָה״ (Deuteronomy 2). But the Midianites took up a quarrel that was not theirs. Another interpretation: on account of two fine foals that I have to bring forth from them — Ruth the Moabitess and Naamah the Ammonitess (Bava Kama 38)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:20.312664059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}